- You have atrial fibrillation or another arrhythmia requiring specialized management.
- You have structural heart disease (valve disease, prior MI, heart failure) or new symptoms (persistent palpitations, syncope, chest pain, unexplained exertional shortness of breath).
- You have complex anticoagulation needs, recurrent bleeding while on anticoagulant, or unclear anticoagulation management (e.g., switching between warfarin and direct oral anticoagulants).
